## RuleGuard: Business Rule Conflict Detection and Resolution System

### Project Overview

RuleGuard is a Python-based software development project designed to help organizations identify problems in business rules before those rules are used in real business processes. Organizations often maintain rules from different departments, and these rules may overlap, contradict each other, or contain conditions that can never be reached. When these problems are not identified, they can lead to incorrect decisions and make business rule maintenance more difficult. RuleGuard will provide a system that allows users to enter, organize, and review business rules and identify potential problems before they affect business processes.

### Problem Statement

Business rules are used by organizations to support decisions and processes, but maintaining multiple rules can become difficult when rules are created or updated at different times. Two rules may apply to the same situation while producing different decisions, or one rule may contain conditions that are already covered by another rule. There may also be rules with conditions that cannot be reached. Manually checking these relationships can require significant effort, especially as the number of rules increases. RuleGuard will address this problem by providing a structured way to compare business rules and identify potential conflicts.

### Project Goal

The main goal of RuleGuard is to develop an application that can analyze business rules and help users identify overlapping conditions, contradictory decisions, and unreachable rules. The system will not only identify that a problem exists but will also show the rules and conditions involved so users can understand why the issue was detected. The application will also support testing of different rule combinations so users can understand which rules would be applied in different situations.

### System Requirements

RuleGuard will allow users to enter, edit, and organize business rules using a structured format. Each rule will contain information such as conditions, operators, values, and expected decisions. The system will compare these rules and identify situations where conditions overlap or where different rules can produce contradictory decisions. It will also identify rules that contain conditions that cannot be reached. In addition, the system will generate test cases for important combinations of conditions and show which rules would be applied. Users will be able to review detected conflicts, inspect the affected rules, and mark issues as resolved after reviewing them.

### Organizational Usefulness

The system is intended to help organizations find business rule problems earlier in the rule-management process. By identifying potential conflicts before rules are used in real processes, RuleGuard can help reduce incorrect decisions caused by inconsistent policies. The system can also make rule maintenance easier by giving users a structured way to review existing rules and understand how a new or changed rule may affect other rules. Providing clear explanations of detected conflicts can help users understand the issue instead of only receiving a general warning that a conflict exists.

### Expected Advantages

I expect RuleGuard to help reduce the amount of manual checking required when reviewing business rules. The system can help users identify problems earlier, improve confidence in the consistency of organizational policies, and make it easier to review changes to existing rules. The test-case functionality will also help users understand how different combinations of conditions affect rule decisions. Overall, the system is intended to provide a practical way to analyze business rules and support better rule maintenance.

### Technology and Resources

I will develop RuleGuard using Python, Streamlit, SQLite, and free Python libraries. Python will be used for the application and rule-processing logic, while Streamlit will provide the user interface. SQLite will be used for local data storage. The application will be developed and demonstrated on my laptop using locally created sample business rule sets. The project will not require external services, and the rule comparison and conflict-detection logic will be implemented as part of the application.

### Project Scope

The initial scope of RuleGuard will focus on entering and managing structured business rules, comparing rules, detecting overlapping conditions, identifying contradictory decisions, finding unreachable rules, generating test cases, and allowing users to review and resolve identified issues. The project will use sample rule sets to demonstrate these capabilities. The system will be developed as a local application and will not depend on external organizational systems or services. The implementation and testing may be refined during development as different rule combinations are evaluated.

### Project Outcome

The expected outcome of the project is a working Python-based prototype that demonstrates how business rules can be analyzed for common conflicts before they are used in business processes. The final system will provide a Streamlit interface for managing and reviewing rules, SQLite for local storage, and rule-processing functionality for detecting and explaining potential problems. The project will be tested using different rule combinations, including overlapping, contradictory, and unreachable rules, to demonstrate the usefulness of the system.
